1. Vendored Cellpose Appose scripts (BSD-3-Clause)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following Python scripts and pixi manifest, bundled under
    src/main/resources/qupath/ext/biop/cellpose/appose/
        cp3.py
        cp4.py
        cp_utils.py
        cp3_init.py
        cp4_init.py
        pixi.toml
are vendored (with their original license headers preserved) from the
imglib2-cellpose project:

    Project : imglib2-cellpose
    Source  : https://github.com/Image-Analysis-Hub/imglib2-cellpose
    Commit  : 95d6f221ad099eb3731fa8afbced80b56d62eeb6
    License : BSD-3-Clause

The Python scripts are byte-identical to that commit. pixi.toml carries ONE
modification, marked by a comment in the file: its `default` environment is
empty rather than `["cp3", "cu126"]`. Appose runs `pixi install` with no
--environment before activating a named one, so the default environment is
installed on every machine; as inherited, that meant every machine downloaded a
CUDA PyTorch, including machines that go on to use the CPU environment and can
never run it. The accompanying pixi.lock is generated from this manifest and is
not part of the upstream project.

In addition, the Appose environment-build and service/model lifecycle used by the
in-process backend (the classes ApposeBackend and ApposeEnvironments under
    src/main/java/qupath/ext/biop/cellpose/backend/)
were adapted, with attribution, from the same imglib2-cellpose project
(net.imglib2.cellpose.Cellpose and net.imglib2.cellpose.CellposeRunner). The
BufferedImage/ImageProcessor <-> Appose NDArray marshalling (the NDArrays class)
is independent original work written against the public Appose NDArray API and does
not reuse the ImgLib2 RAI/appose bridge.

