2. Appose (BSD-2-Clause)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The in-process backend uses Appose (org.apposed:appose:0.12.0) for building the
Python environment and exchanging data through shared memory.

    Project : Appose
    Source  : https://github.com/apposed/appose
    License : BSD-2-Clause

Appose and its transitive dependencies (Apache Ivy, Apache Commons Compress, JNA)
are consumed as unmodified binary dependencies under their respective licenses.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Apache Groovy JSON module (Apache-2.0)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Appose's Java-side worker protocol needs groovy.json.JsonOutput. QuPath ships
Groovy core but not the groovy-json module, so it is added as an explicit
dependency, pinned to QuPath's own Groovy version.

    Project : Apache Groovy (groovy-json)
    Source  : https://groovy.apache.org
    License : Apache-2.0

It is consumed as an unmodified binary dependency.
